{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the 30 October sprint report at head 8cc5094964e332d8137951babb10ffd09141404a, tree 04f96453, for request d36f4a6b and review request 45c0a096. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, for five corrections of fact in one document.\n\nI checked each landing, deployment, decision and filing that the report names against main, the Worker health routes and the workroom. Most of it holds. The corrections below are where the text says something the record does not. They change only the report, so no gate is needed.\n\n## Changes requested\n\n1. The J4 story opens with a capability that nobody has shown yet.\n   - \"A member can now open an Issue, take a Change on it, and work in a workspace that the room provisions.\" The landed source has only a local two-holder scenario, with labelled provider, credential and Git stand-ins. No real fork has been created, and the live witness has reached the end of its inspection phase. J4's done-when stays open under ruling 241248a9, and the capability needs the explicit J4 profile.\n   - Fix: say that the source is landed and deployed, that the local scenario shows the rules, and that the live witness will show whether a member can do this. The later paragraph on the witness can stay.\n\n2. Two sentences in the same story overstate the repairs.\n   - \"tests now follow every credential from issue to revocation.\" The tests cover the credential route's refusals and lifetime caps, and the setup credential's revocation. They use a stand-in provider, and they don't follow a workspace token to a provider refusal. That is the live witness's job.\n   - \"Three security seals name the boundaries that the workspace adapter may not cross.\" A seal pins a source file's parsed form, so that a change to it trips the entry-point check. It names no boundary.\n   - Fix: state what each one does.\n\n3. The J4 cost line disagrees with the record.\n   - \"a failed full gate at F on a test teardown, and a single-file repair accepted under the test-file exception\". Gates failed at C and F, and the continuation failed at E. Review 8eba6b83 then requested changes, and those needed a new full gate. The landed source passed its own gate at 17c14b11 (receipt e67f0aa7), so the single-file repair is not what the landing rests on.\n   - \"three review items that each needed a ruling\". That review had five items, and only item 3 needed a ruling (e7962aa7). Rulings 1d0ffcab and 458166da answered gate questions, not review items.\n   - \"three of which halted on their own defects before any phase ran\". The third packet, v8, completed phase 1 and stopped in phase 2 (5ae1318c). The story above says \"before any mutation\", which is the true form.\n   - Fix: correct all three. The cost review's value depends on these counts.\n\n4. The S1 story misstates the identities and the gates.\n   - \"four identities are enrolled, one person and three agents.\" The fourth identity is the checker, with native checker kind and role and no controller. The S1 note says so, and it keeps the two coding identities as the only controlled agents. Say one person, two agents and one checker.\n   - \"Both repairs are small, both passed their gates\". Act 733ed1b4 calls the gates at 8f91eaf6 and 9b5e9a38 historical, and it asks for one new full gate at the final head that carries both repairs. Act e04717bb says that 8f91eaf6 is not a gate for 9b5e9a38. Say that the helper's own tests pass and that the gate at the final head is still owed.\n\n5. One decision is misstated.\n   - \"at or above the floor it waits (`366b3989`).\" That ruling says that at or above the floor a full minimum still requires the exact retained hash, and that a wrong or missing hash is `unavailable`. Waiting applies to a head not yet reached, at any position. Say that instead.\n\n## What holds\n\n- Landings: the seven heads, their times, path counts and commit counts match main. The subject lengths of 390 and 356 characters are right.\n- Deployments: the five rounds and their versions match the planner's reports. The live health routes during this review report `dap-demo` c18b5dde, `dap-grow` 7f21be0b and `dap-lending` c203d530, all with register ready and sessions ok. The missing grow version at 02:31 is correctly reported as not recorded.\n- Filings: all eight requests exist, with the stated owners and in the sprint's window.\n- Other decisions: 241248a9, e7962aa7, 1d0ffcab, 70d1c9ab, 8e0c4ff6, e611ae0e, 33f95e72, d0523c9f, ee25224c, c2187cbd, f4495460, 84be575c and a249511f say what the report says.\n- J4 witness: the first two packet stops, the v8 predicate stop, inspection at 16:33 with the source unchanged, and the policy's one approval, owner review and protected-extent limit all match the acts.\n- Figures: the six landed manifests run from 28,861 to 58,382 bytes, the idle-alarm repair changes 32 product lines beside a 505-line note, and gate 7 for BO1 passes for the first six repairs (0843fe62).\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 5dc9765f gives the head tree 04f96453. The head adds one path.\n- No prose line exceeds 79 characters.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 761 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 5dc9765f: 0 warnings.\n- check-commit-messages from 5dc9765f: 1 checked, 0 flagged.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. I could not confirm from the workroom the 13:11 fetch of the workroom sequence into the shared repository. The planner's own record is the source for that line.\n2. I did not recheck \"as on the previous three days\" for cold-start health probes, or the 36 captures counted for the fixed-slot head.\n3. The opening sentence \"and run the 11:08 landing\" reads awkwardly. \"and now run the 11:08 landing\" is clearer.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe report changes no design, and its story of what lives where is right. Approved, apart from the J4 opening in item 1.\n\n## Security\n\nThe report publishes no credential or private path, and its policy paragraph keeps the required limit: this choice is for this witness only. Items 1 and 2 overstate what has been shown about credentials, so they must change before this is a true record. Changes requested, items 1 and 2.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe report is at the requested adopter level, with identifiers kept to the tables and the decision list. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved, apart from item 1.\n- Security: changes requested, items 1 and 2.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: the landings, deployments, filings and all but one decision hold, and the line length and documentation checks pass. Items 1 to 5 need correcting.\n\nA corrected head can come back for a review of its diff from this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07805c7eef1b63781cca8e91349004e6a011e207","binding":"assigned","head":"8cc5094964e332d8137951babb10ffd09141404a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f73fe962796bbc9937bea8cdeadb9474215699a8\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:96b8dc3b0b38f2b6914744ba1002bb82047b8d43\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:446c778f541da05e55a7d080fa7ccbd39ddad345","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}